WEBVTT

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.710
Don't underestimate me. I'm still an instructor.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.460
Where are you, Tsubaki-chan?!

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.120
Here, Kotecchan!

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.540
Tsubaki wins!

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.150
This was all I could come up with.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.170
Not bad.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.680
That's enough, Haru!

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.810
Not bad, Akira.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.020
Maybe I'll go all out, too!

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.910
It would've been nice to run
with you more, Akira.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.960
Sorry, Haru...

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.970
You can't beat Chiyu.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.100
Cut the bullshit!

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.870
And in the end, it was just as planned.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.570
We've always been broken.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.740
Nationalist dog!

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.830
You're just a mutt sniffing around, yourself.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.370
Not bad. I'm impressed.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.180
You're as strong as ever.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.890
That hurts.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.520
Sorry. Looks like we both need healing.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.900
Listen to your requiem.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.490
I won't hold back!

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.410
You've wronged your country!

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.710
Suruga!

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.670
Sorry. Did that hurt?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.770
The death god's scythe reaches all.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.050
A secret arrow.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.900
I see...

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.590
Was this the only way?

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.640
Fate is a shadowy figure.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.130
Chase after it, and it runs.
Run, and it chases you.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.760
Are we evil?

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.510
Who knows? I certainly don't.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.580
Can we correct this twisted fate?

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.180
I don't know.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.210
Yuri.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.850
Chihiro-kun.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.970
Our Lives We Pay Our Enemies

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.220
Domyoji Dojo

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.860
Enough!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.740
Life and death are two faces of the same coin

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.740
Oh, come on.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.050
You keep going for the <i>kote</i>.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:56.320
Go for the <i>men</i>, Chihiro-san.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.540
A win is a win, Kotetsu.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.210
Complaining about a loss
reveals your immaturity.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.370
Dad.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.810
It's the mystery of non-killing.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.930
Stealing your opponent's
strength and using it to win

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.040
is the greatest essence of swordplay.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:18.730
In a real battle, you won't be able to
defeat your opponents with <i>kote</i> strikes.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.690
I know.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.870
Let's go again, Chihiro-san.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.570
Sorry. I have to get ready.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.230
No fair! You're just quitting after you win?

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.160
You don't want breakfast?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.040
I don't know what to do with him.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:45.880
If only he'd change his mind,
I could live in easy retirement.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.660
Your rolled omelets are the best, Chihiro-san.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.210
You can't live without them, Kotetsu.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.180
They're so fluffy...

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.970
I know. You stirred them a hundred times, right?

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:12.450
The secret is watching the heat
and not stirring too much.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:16.470
I don't need to know that. I just eat.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.690
You should at least learn to cook.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.590
Why? I've got you.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.590
What am I, your wife?

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.980
Yeah, why not?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.760
We'll take over the dojo together.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.970
You'll be the instructor,
and I'll be your assistant.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.860
What do you think, Dad?

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.670
I prefer hot spring eggs.

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:41.330
That's not what I'm asking.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.260
Then we'll have hot spring eggs tomorrow.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.420
If we're going to be instructors,

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.060
we'll have to be good
examples to our students.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.200
You'll need to show them how strong you are.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.220
Get a good <i>men</i> hit in.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.570
You're stronger than me in matches.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.750
Huh? I'm strong?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.580
Seriously?

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.810
I've never beaten you, though.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.500
Chihiro-san, are you really leaving?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.300
Yeah, I guess.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.680
Why? What's there to complain about?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.430
I don't have any complaints.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:26.620
Since you took me in, I've felt nothing
but gratitude for you and your father.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.850
He raised me until now.
He even sent me to college.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:32.150
But...

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.450
But what?

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:36.450
"To be or not to be."

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.230
Shakespeare again?

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:40.460
Answer the question, Chihiro-san.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.810
I shouldn't have told you.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.410
I'm just thinking about it for now.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.210
What's going to happen to the dojo?

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.170
Is that why?

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:56.000
I knew there was some reason
you were so persistent today.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.320
Yeah, but...

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.720
I haven't decided yet.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.480
Don't tell your dad.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.590
Chihiro-san!

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:10.920
Ikuro.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.180
Iku-san, good morning.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.200
We have first period free.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.760
Let's go to the cafeteria.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:19.890
We ate already.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.700
Well, I haven't!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.440
They serve ginger-fried pork
on Thursday mornings, right?

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.080
I always eat here.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.270
Sounds like a heavy breakfast.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.260
Okay, I'm in!

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.050
You already ate.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.420
We're the only ones with first period off.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.870
Go to class, first-year.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.840
Don't be mean, Senpai.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.760
What is this?

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.940
I'm covering my ears, but I can still hear it.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:56.360
Ikuro!

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.370
C-Chihiro-san...

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:01.880
Kotetsu?!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.330
Hang in there!

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:24.830
That sound...

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.830
"We are such stuff as dreams are made on."

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.070
"Yea, all which it inherit, shall dissolve,

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.540
And, like this insubstantial pageant faded,

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:22.610
Leave not a rack behind."

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.900
<i>The Tempest</i>, huh?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.750
Which means this is all a dream.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:35.750
Fate, continuously woven from a thread
of intertwining good and evil.

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.430
What are you trying to say?

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:39.650
Don't you like it?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.200
They're all words that are inside you.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.040
Even theater can be a killjoy
if it's taken too far.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:52.130
I like Shakespeare, but
I don't like seeing it twisted so.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:56.140
Man of vermilion.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.270
Heroic power resides in your blood.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:03.910
The king imprisoned on a desert island
in a distant sea puts his subjects to work,

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:06.200
continuously searching for answers.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.910
What are you talking about?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.400
Who are you?

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:12.630
I am Dux.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.220
Until the end of time,

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:22.180
we will repeat this heroic
scene again and again

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:25.810
in the words of nations not yet known.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.190
Inuki, he's awake!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.640
The Sleeping Prince is finally awake.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.490
Did you give him a magic kiss?

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:47.620
Yeah, right!

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.360
I'm joking.

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.530
Check his consciousness levels.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.790
Hey, hot stuff.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.250
You're the last one.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:59.550
Do you know who you are?

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.580
I... I...

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.660
Don't tell me you have amnesia.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:08.050
Kamina.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.090
I'm Kamina Chihiro.

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:12.180
Okay, good.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.560
That's what the student ID you had says, too.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:19.140
Jokei University second-year
student, English department...

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.390
What happened to me—

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.710
Don't interrupt!

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:25.590
That's what you call impolite.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.530
Don't hit the patient. That's also impolite.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.530
Shut up.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:32.950
Where are we?

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.640
The Jokei University hospital.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.960
I'm the attending physician, Akaya Inuki.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.240
This is Sakiyama Koume.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.840
Don't call me a "this."

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:47.870
So, Sleeping Prince, you've
been asleep for five months.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:49.350
Did you know that?

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.650
Five months?! You can't be serious.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:55.670
Most people woke up within a week.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.170
Now, what did you dream about?

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.310
Dream?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.860
Dreams of another world.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:04.800
Dreams in which you became something else.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.900
Something else?

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.110
Um, what are you talking about?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:14.160
A lot of people mentioned it after they
lost consciousness in the Great Collapse.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.120
"The Great Collapse?"

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.870
It'd be quicker for you to see for yourself.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:37.310
What is this?

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.000
Tokyo after the Great Collapse.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.880
What is this Great Collapse?

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:47.120
You must've heard that strange
sound before you collapsed.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:51.150
We still don't know what it was.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:55.970
When we woke up, that giant plant had grown

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.880
and we were enveloped in a red mist.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:04.460
We have no way of knowing what
happened during that week.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.840
That's the Great Collapse.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.400
What is that plant?

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.390
What happened to Tokyo?!

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:13.760
Oh, shut up!

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:18.220
It's too difficult to explain.
Ask your friend about it.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.950
You can come in now.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.020
Thank goodness! I'm so glad you're okay!

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.890
They wouldn't let me see you.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.180
Your nurse is astoundingly rude, too.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.660
What was that?

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.990
If they'd dissected you,

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.850
I swore I'd avenge you before
committing ritual suicide.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.830
What era are you from, exactly?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:44.020
He's always like this.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:47.090
He's been underfoot every day.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.420
Sorry. You must've been worried.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.650
I'm surprised I can walk.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:01.270
Everyone who passed out during the
Great Collapse is surprisingly healthy.

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.850
I couldn't believe I'd been asleep for a week.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.740
Congratulations on your
recovery, Kamina Chihiro-kun.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.940
Kakihara-san.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.990
What are you doing here?

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.450
Journalists have a keen nose.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:23.500
"Post-Great Collapse, the last
comatose individual finally awakes."

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.960
There's the headline.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.170
Why were you asleep for five months?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.010
Hey!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.980
Did you not bring enough people down with you?

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:35.510
Or is it no fun unless you kill them yourself?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:38.470
Like you did 13 years ago.

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:42.600
That's enough!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.720
Why are you always following
Chihiro-san around?

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:49.230
You make it sound bad. It's my job.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.130
I'll leave it at that,

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:55.040
including the truth about
what happened 13 years ago.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.000
So scary.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.610
Let's go, Tsubasa.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.540
Five months after the Great Collapse,
"Save Tokyo" demonstrations

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:15.410
are being held in the capital of Osaka.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.280
The government is sending
trillions of yen in food

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:23.430
and medical assistance to the special
autonomous district of Tokyo,

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.520
What will happen to Tokyo?!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.520
Special autonomous district?

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.940
That's what they're calling Tokyo now.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.860
however, many issues still remain...

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:28.040
No one can get out because of the red mist.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.300
What do you mean?

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:31.270
That's the red mist.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:33.030
Can you see it?

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:40.440
There are colonies all over the place,
but it encompasses all of Tokyo.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.500
Red mist...

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:48.420
I heard you could get in and out at first, but...

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.880
Now everyone stays away.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.550
They say no one's been able
to pass through the red mist.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.550
It was already like this
by the time I woke up.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.800
There was a lot of confusion.

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:02.480
You can't leave,

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.440
but the power and water's flowing.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.160
Home's where you make it.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.280
I see.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.370
You just got out of the hospital.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.610
You should sleep until we get home.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:16.820
You're right.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.660
I'll do that.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.700
The dojo?

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.550
What is this?

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.090
Sir!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.710
What was that?

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:44.580
Are you okay?

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.350
Yeah.

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.350
How's your dad?

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.350
My dad? He's doing great.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.450
Domyoji Dojo

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:07.140
You're finally home.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:09.420
I feel strange.

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:12.080
It's like I just left this morning.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.460
This sound...

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:21.660
What is this?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.470
My body feels hot...

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:47.210
Is he making this sound?

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.520
Dad?

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:16.440
Run!

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:18.640
The instructor...

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.760
Is that... your dad?

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:24.950
Dammit, what's going on?!

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:37.520
Chihiro-san!

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:02.370
You can't defeat your
opponents with kote<i> strikes.</i>

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.030
Chihiro-san!
